  abstract = {Motivation: In many organisms, including humans, recombination
              clusters within recombination hotspots. The standard method for de
              novo detection of recombinants at hotspots is sperm typing. This
              relies on allele-specific PCR at single nucleotide polymorphisms.
              Designing allele-specific primers by hand is time-consuming. We
              have therefore written a package to support hotspot detection and
              analysis.Results: hotspot consists of four programs: asp looks up
              SNPs and designs allele-specific primers; aso constructs
              allele-specific oligos for mapping recombinants; xov implements a
              maximum-likelihood method for estimating the crossover rate; six,
              finally, simulates typing data.Availability and Implementation:
              hotspot is written in C. Sources are freely available under the GNU
